.page adduser 8 add a resident to the Human Village

# SYNOPSIS
*adduser* [*-c* _FULLNAME_] [*-s* _SHELL_] [*-L*] [*--no-seat*] _NAME_

# DESCRIPTION
`adduser` creates an account. It adds a line for _NAME_ to `/Hakurei/etc/passwd`, `/Hakurei/etc/shadow` and `/Hakurei/etc/group` and makes the home directory `/HumanVillage/`_NAME_. The user and a group of the same name get the next free number from 1000 upward. Only root may do it (try `sudo adduser`).

Unless `-L` is given, `adduser` asks for a password twice; an empty answer means an account without a password. If the two answers differ nothing is created.

_NAME_ must start with a lower case letter or `_`, may contain only lower case letters, digits, `_` and `-`, and may be at most 31 characters long. A name that is already taken is refused.

The new account joins the group `shrine`, which is what gives a user a seat at the desktop. Use `--no-seat` to leave it out.

# OPTIONS
@ *-c* _FULLNAME_
    The full name, kept in the comment field of the user database. The default is _NAME_ with a capital first letter.
@ *-s* _SHELL_
    The login shell. The default is `/bin/gapsh`.
@ *-L*
    Create the account locked: no password is asked for and nobody can log in to it until a password is set.
@ *--no-seat*
    Do not put the user into the group `shrine`: the account gets no desktop.

# EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if the account could not be created (not root, a bad or taken name, passwords that differ, a file that could not be written); 2 for a usage error.

# EXAMPLES
    sudo adduser -c "Alice Margatroid" alice
    sudo adduser -L --no-seat nobody2

# FILES
@ /Hakurei/etc/passwd, /Hakurei/etc/shadow, /Hakurei/etc/group
    The databases that are edited. Each is replaced in one step and, with a HUMANVILLAGE volume, kept on it as well (etckeep(8)), so the change survives a restart.
@ /HumanVillage
    Where home directories are made.

# SEE ALSO
deluser(8), passwd(5), group(5)
